Turns out all I was missing was a type="source". The command:
install.packages("tikzDevice", repos="http://R-forge.R-project.org", type="source")
should work fine.

There's a handy blog article about getting knitr to work with R 3.0 here <http://enoriver.net/index.php/2013/04/12/keeping-knitr-happy-after-upgrading-to-r-3-0-0/>.

